Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 05:40:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] x1600: add SFC driver

Keep the SFC functional clock gated while the controller is idle.
Enable it only while configuring a device or executing a SPI memory
request. Mask and drain interrupts, then synchronize the IRQ before
disabling the clock. Initialize the controller to a stopped, masked
state before registering its interrupt handler.
---
 drivers/spi/Kconfig           |    9 +
 drivers/spi/Makefile          |    1 +
 drivers/spi/spi-ingenic-sfc.c | 1107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1117 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/spi/spi-ingenic-sfc.c

diff --git a/drivers/spi/Kconfig b/drivers/spi/Kconfig
index 1872f9d54..864e2b292 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/spi/Kconfig
@@ -518,6 +518,15 @@ config SPI_INGENIC
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called spi-ingenic.
 
+config SPI_INGENIC_SFC
+        tristate "Ingenic SoCs SPI SFC controller"
+        depends on MACH_INGENIC || COMPILE_TEST
+        help
+          This enables support for the Ingenic SoCs SPI SFC controller.
+
+          To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
+          will be called spi-ingenic.
+
 config SPI_INTEL
 	tristate
 
